3. The brief facts of the present case are that on 26.06.1999, the food officials consisting of Food Inspectors Sh. Jeet Ram and Sh Gian Chand under the supervision of Local Health Authority/SDM Sh. R.P. Meena reached at Khajuri Khas, Wazirabad Road, where they CA no. 8738/16 Sukhpal Singh & Anrs Vs. Delhi Admn /Food Inspector (PFA) Pages 2 of 15 found a tanker bearing No. HR 38-C-2878 has stored the food article i.e. 'standardized Milk' in its tanker for sale purpose for the use of human consumption ; accused no. 1 Sh. Balraj (since Proclaimed Offender) was the driver of the said tanker and it was found that the milk was being carried for sale in Delhi ; the sample of milk was then lifted as per procedure prescribed under the PFA Act and Rules ; each sample was separately packed, fastened, marked, sealed and necessary documents were prepared at the spot including the Notice as per Form-VI, panchnama etc in the presence of appellant/ accused ; that the price of the sample was paid to the vendor who disclosed that the milk belongs to accused no.2 company i.e. M/s Gopaljee G.K. Dairy & Milk Product (P) Ltd., a partnership Company ; that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA) in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 12.07.1999, PA found the sample to be not conforming to the standards because 'milk solids not fat', it was found to be having 7.02% which was less than the prescribed minimum limit of 8.5% ;
- that upon receipt of report, the SDM/LHA ordered investigation which was carried out by Food Inspector and it was revealed that the milk in the tanker belonged to the appellant no2/accused no 2, Company, having two Directors namely Sh Pyare Mohan Dixit and Sh. Radhey Shyam Dixit, and the said company had appointed the appellant no.1 /accused no.3 Mr. Sukhpal Singh, as its Nominee under section 17 PF Act, and as such he was deemed to be in CA no. 8738/16 Sukhpal Singh & Anrs Vs. Delhi Admn /Food Inspector (PFA) Pages 3 of 15 charge of and responsible for the affair of business of their above mentioned company ; that after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.
